The 20-second storyline: "The Flavour Switch"

0–3 sec | The tease
A bowl of ordinary noodles appears. The camera slowly pushes in.
Text: "Your noodles deserve more..."

3–7 sec | The secret ingredient
A Knorr Chicken cube spins into the frame. Its wrapper opens, and the cube crumbles into seasoning particles.
Text: "Just a little Knorr magic."

7–13 sec | The transformation
The seasoning falls into the noodles. On the beat drop, everything transforms into rich, glossy, spicy noodles. Peppers and vegetables fly into place. Steam rises.
Text: "Now we're talking!"

13–17 sec | The craving shot
Chopsticks lift the noodles in slow motion, with a beautiful sauce-coated noodle pull.
Text: "Rich flavour. Every bite."

17–20 sec | The hero reveal
The Knorr Chicken pack lands beside the finished noodles. The background transitions into Knorr green and yellow.
Final text: "KNORR. Taste the difference."

Creative direction
Use the images I uploaded as the actual visual references, particularly the noodle-lifting photographs and the clean Knorr packshots.
The motion should feel like a professional food commercial, not a slideshow: seamless match cuts, realistic ingredient movement, controlled speed ramps, subtle camera movement, and close-up food textures.
Sound is important: start with a quiet kitchen ambience, introduce a wrapper-tearing sound and seasoning crumble, then drop into upbeat Nigerian Afrobeats as the noodles transform. Finish with a short, satisfying sonic logo.
Make it 9:16 vertical, 1080 × 1920, suitable for Instagram Reels, TikTok, and YouTube Shorts.
The most important transition is at 7 seconds. The cube crumbles, the music drops, and the ordinary noodles become irresistible. That single moment should make the advert memorable.
